{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001189","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00001189","description":["A food product made from oats."],"label":"oat food product","obo_id":"FOODON:00001189","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["common oat food product"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00002062","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00002062","description":["A food product made from milled oats."],"label":"milled oat food product","obo_id":"FOODON:00002062","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001759","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00001759","description":[],"label":"common oat cereal food product","obo_id":"FOODON:00001759","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03306272","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03306272","description":["Milled and reconstructed flakes made from oats and usually served as a cold cereal product.","SIREN DB annotation:\n* whole, shape achieved by forming, thickness \u003c0.3 cm. FOODON:03430153\n* fully heat-treated FOODON:03440014\n* seed, skin removed, germ present FOODON:03420132\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* food flaking process FOODON:03460274\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"oat flakes","obo_id":"FOODON:03306272","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400816","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400816","description":["LanguaL curation note: Excludes rolled oats, corn grits and similar products, which are indexed under *RICE OR OTHER GRAIN *.","Prepared grain product ready or nearly ready for consumption and marketed primarily for breakfast use. Includes formulated breakfast cereals such as \u0027corn flakes\u0027 or \"muesli\" and simple breakfast cereals such as instant oatmeal."],"label":"breakfast cereal (eurofir)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400816","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03510214","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03510214","description":["Regulated by Directive 2003/89/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 10 November 2003 amending Directive 2000/13/EC as regards indication of the ingredients present in foodstuffs.\n\nLanguaL curation note: Used for cereals containing gluten ( i.e. wheat, rye, barley, oats, spelt, kamut or their hybridised strains) and products thereof"],"label":"food allergen labelling about cereals containing gluten and products thereof","obo_id":"FOODON:03510214","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400972","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400972","description":["Includes any products that can be described/observed as a processed cereal produced from wheat, rye, barley, oats, or other types of grain, which has gone through further manufacturing processes such as cooking and milling, which does not require cooking","LanguaL curation note: Index type of cereal/grain (barley, rice) in facet B.  Index claims (organic, low calorie, sugar free or low) in facet P. If ingredient added (sugar), index in facet H. Index preservation method (refrigeration) in facet J."],"label":"10000286 - cereal products - ready to eat (perishable) (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400972","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400970","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400970","description":["Includes any products that can be described/observed as a cereal combining all or some of the following ingredients: oats, muesli, wheat, rice, seeds, bran, fruit, nuts, cereal and honey, which has gone through further manufacturing processes such as cook","LanguaL curation note: Index type of cereal/grain (barley, rice) in facet B.  Index claims (organic, low calorie, sugar free or low) in facet P. If ingredient added (sugar), index in facet H."],"label":"10000285 - cereals products - not ready to eat (shelf stable) (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400970","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400971","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400971","description":["Includes any products that can be described/observed as a cereal combining all or some of the following ingredients; oats, muesli, wheat, rice, seeds, bran, fruit, nuts, cereal and honey, which has gone through further manufacturing processes such as cook","LanguaL curation note: Index type of cereal/grain (barley, rice) in facet B.  Index claims (organic, low calorie, sugar free or low) in facet P. If ingredient added (sugar), index in facet H."],"label":"10000284 - cereals products - ready to eat (shelf stable) (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400971","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03401776","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03401776","description":["Includes any product that can be described/observed as a cereal combining all or some of the following ingredients: oats, muesli, wheat, rice, seeds, bran, fruit, nuts, cereal and honey, which has gone through further manufacturing processes such as cooki","LanguaL curation note: Index cereal type in facet B. Index calorie, sweetener and organic claims in facet P."],"label":"10006250 - cereals products - not ready to eat (frozen) (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03401776","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400973","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400973","description":["Includes any products that can be described/observed as a block or bar combining all or some of the following ingredients; oats, muesli, wheat, rice, bran, seeds, fruit, nuts, cereal and honey. Products may contain chocolate or be fully or partially choco","LanguaL curation note: Index claims (organic, low calorie, sugar free or low) in facet P. If ingredient added (fruit, sugar) or surface coated/filled, index in facet H."],"label":"10000287 - cereal/muesli bars (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400973","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400814","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400814","description":["Examples are whole grain wheat, brown rice, bulgur, parboiled rice, rolled oats, wild rice, pearl barley, millet, rolled oats, corn grits and similar products."],"label":"rice or other grain (eurofir)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400814","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400258","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400258","description":["Prepared grain product ready or nearly ready for consumption and marketed primarily for breakfast use. Includes formulated breakfast cereals such as \u0027corn flakes\u0027 or \u0027cheerios\u0027 and simple breakfast cereals such as instant oatmeal. Excludes rolled oats, corn grits and similar products, which are indexed under *MILLED GRAIN OR STARCH PRODUCT*. See also *MILLED GRAIN OR STARCH PRODUCT*."],"label":"breakfast cereal (us cfr)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400258","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03420133","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03420133","description":["LanguaL curation note: In the case of grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*), the descriptor can be used to describe whole grains, which may include  may include amaranth, barley, buckwheat, bulgur, corn (including popcorn), millet, quinoa, rice, rye, oats, sorghum, teff, triticale, wheat, and wild rice.*\nRenamed from *SEED OR KERNEL, SKIN PRESENT, GERM PRESENT* in LanguaL 2008.","Whole grains are cereal grains (NT of *GRAIN [B1324]*) that consist of the intact, ground, cracked or flaked caryopsis, whose principal anatomical components - the starchy endosperm, germ and bran - are present in the same relative proportions as they exist in the intact caryopsis - should be considered a whole grain food.\nThis definition means that 100% of the original kernel all of the bran, germ, and endosperm must be present to qualify as a whole grain.\nWhole grains or foods made from them contain all the essential parts and naturally-occurring nutrients of the entire grain seed. If the grain has been processed (e.g., cracked, crushed, rolled, extruded, and/or cooked), the food product should deliver approximately the same rich balance of nutrients that are found in the original grain seed.[http://www.fda.gov/Food/GuidanceComplianceRegulatoryInformation/GuidanceDocuments/FoodLabelingNutrition/ucm059088.htm]"],"label":"seed, skin present, germ present","obo_id":"FOODON:03420133","type":"class"}],"numFound":14,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["FOODON","14"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","14"],"ontologyId":["foodon","14","ecto","5","enm","1","envo","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","14"],"isObsolete":["false","14","true","1"],"type":["class","14"]}}}